A1. A place with a spring of mineral water. ~ SPA
A4. Something go-getters get in the morning. ~ UP
A6. A public announcement. ~ AD
A7. Where old flames have gone since the beginning of time. ~ OUT
A10. These often get lit at night. ~ LAMPS
A12. A chorus girl's support. ~ LEG
A13. What a husband tells his wife when he comes floating home at 3 A.M. ~ TALES
A15. King of Bashan. ~ OG
A16. Something a wild woman isn't. ~ TAME
A17. A good place to go if you want to get a drink on the house. ~ ROOF
A18. Feminine affirmative. ~ NO
A19. What go-getters do. ~ GET
A21. Born. ~ NEE
A22. This goes with a dash. ~ DOT
A23. Futile attempt of a tenant when his rent is raised. ~ SUBLET
A24. A good season for hard-boiled eggs. (Not salt.) ~ EASTER
A26. A very easy word to say. ~ YES
A29. Webster says this means "to repair frequently"; we assure you, however, it has nothing to do with second-hand cars. ~ RESORT
A33. About the only good thing you can get a lot of that's absolutely free. ~ ADVICE
A36. Inventor of the bedtime story. (Ask any married man.) ~ AESOP
A37. A mushroom. ~ PARLOR
A40. A good thing to hold your best girl in. ~ ESTEEM
A44. Something that can always be found near the seashore during the summer months. ~ SEA
A46. Place where pedestrians come to their own conclusions. ~ STREET
A47. There's many a slip about this. ~ PILLOW
A49. Part of the verb to have. ~ HAS
A50. Something Brutus tried to borrow. ~ EAR
A51. A weak-end covering. ~ WIG
A53. French masculine pronoun. ~ IL
A54. This is the cat's. ~ MEOW
A55. A musical instrument. Dora thinks this is a person who rides in box cars and cooks in a tin can. ~ OBOE
A57. Virginia (abbr.). ~ VA
A58. A creed, doctrine, principal, opinion, or what have you? ~ TENET
A60. Contraction of "even." ~ EEN
A61. This talks but it usually says "Good-by." ~ MONEY
A63. A famous chip. ~ SON
A64. A sky pilot's title (abbr.). ~ DD
A65. In such manner. ~ SO
A66. National Order of Simps (abbr.). ~ NOS

D1. Men who always agree with their wives. ~ SAGES
D2. This comes after luncheon. ~ PM
D3. Skillful. ~ APT
D5. What one ride in a second-hand car is. ~ PLENTY
D6. Something a woman never does with her husband. ~ AGREES
D7. A dolt. ~ OAF
D8. Useless Lingerie (abbr.). ~ UL
D9. This has a thick head and sings on the slightest provocation. ~ TENOR
D10. Sometimes this has a rough bark. ~ LOG
D11. Something you often see in a sailor suit. ~ SAILOR
D13. What the pedestrian who hesitates is. ~ TOSSED
D14. A guy who can take his liquor, but can't leave it alone. ~ SOT
D20. It's easy to get cleaned in these. ~ TUBS
D22. Half (Fr.) ~ DEMI
D25. Eithers little partner. ~ OR
D27. This means to follow. ~ ENSUE
D28. A very important person. ~ ME
D30. What the age of Elizabeth was. (Nothing to do with sweet sixteen.) ~ ERA
D31. A wise bird. ~ OWL
D32. Baptismal liquid used by Ku Kluxers. ~ TAR
D33. A fellow who is always monkeying around. ~ APE
D34. A tank. ~ VAT
D35. Something a Chinese actor never misses. ~ CUE
D37. The old block itself. ~ PA
D38. These are things we are warned not to get into. (Flivvers is a seven letter word.) ~ RUTS
D39. You'll have to do a lot of scrambling to get this. ~ OMELET
D41. Correct answer to, "How's the world treating you?" ~ SELDOM
D42. Enough. (Poet.) ~ ENOW
D43. The governess of Texas. ~ MA
D44. Nowadays this is what the father who follows in his son's footsteps gets. ~ STEWED
D45. You don't see these hanging around women much these days. ~ APRONS
D46. These are irresistible to the unfair sex. ~ SALES
D48. These may be down, but they're never outtalked. ~ WIVES
D49. "He who gets slapped" gets this. ~ HIT
D52. "He who gets slapped" gets slapped because he gets this. ~ GAY
D54. These hang around women. ~ MEN
D56. A long time. ~ EON
D59. A famous number of bananas. ~ NO
D62. Same as No. 18 horizontal. ~ NO


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
A58: A creed, doctrine, principal, opinion, or what have you? → principle

